# nt.toml — New Theory inference API config for MA2-YAM
#
# This starter uses mock callbacks. No hardware config is required.
# NT_API_KEY is passed via environment variable (not this file):
#
#   export NT_API_KEY=your_key_here
#   python run.py
#
# When you wire real hardware, this file holds site-specific config
# (arm IPs, camera serial numbers, extrinsics). For MA2-YAM hardware
# details see the model page — joint layout (left arm 0-6, right arm
# 7-13, gripper-last) and camera roles (top=overhead, left/right=wrist).
#
# Copy to ~/.config/nt/nt.toml and fill in hardware values when ready:
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/nt
#   cp conf/nt.toml.example ~/.config/nt/nt.toml
